# Update channels (GitHub #476): a Mac on Stable reads Stable's feed (appcast-stable.xml beside the build's own),
# and while Stable is older than the Mac's build, Settings ▸ Advanced offers Stable's disk image, since Sparkle never
# installs an older version. The feeds are scripts/appcast-feeds.py's from Tests/Fixtures/Appcast.
# The channel comes as an argument, so the test never writes the real Cra's settings, and Sparkle doesn't check.
budget rss=600 stalls50=10
env CRA_UPDATE_FEED=${ORIGIN}/updates/appcast.xml
arg -updateChannel
arg stable
arg -SUEnableAutomaticChecks
arg NO
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=kept
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
cra://action/settings
wait 1
cra://debug?settingsPane=advanced
wait 2
expect-log stable release 0\.1\.43, older than this build: yes
